From a32ddca21dbb64799091d6fb51f40b5c708a22bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:11:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec-decode): profile DSpark costs once when pinned
 curves cover the shapes

Upstream base: local-inference-lab/vllm integration/karmic-kraken-beta
04c30fa9 with this deployment's patch series (independent of the
batch-invariance patches).

With SPARK3_DSPARK_COST_DIR set, rank 0 replaces the profiled cost curves
with pinned ones whenever a file matches the profile's shape set, yet the
boot still ran every timed round (5 by default) of both profiling phases,
about 16 s of a ~120 s boot, only to compute that key. Now one timed round
runs first; rank 0 checks for matching pinned curves and broadcasts the
answer, and the remaining rounds run only when none exist. The rounds
continue the alternating shape order, so a completed profile is the same
as one taken in a single block, and a new shape set is still pinned from
the full profile.

Without a cost directory nothing changes. Quality: none (costs only steer
draft budgets, and pinned curves were already used in place of profiled
ones).

Tests: tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py (one-round
boot with pinned curves; split profile equals one block).
Upstream status: local.
